WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.645
A galaxy you can see: its photograph.

00:03.361 --> 00:11.360
From the southern half of the Earth this pale cloud is plain to the eye: the Large Magellanic Cloud, a small galaxy beside ours.

00:12.033 --> 00:16.640
Stars that eclipse each other put it a hundred and sixty thousand light-years away.
